    {
      "ordinal": 5,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "4",
      "title": "Wooden Shields Requirements",
      "body": "The entire edge must be covered with either a band of strong leather, or with at least three or more layers of fabric.\nA leather band must be glued, sewn or riveted, to the Shield. Any rivets must be neatly finished, the edge of the rivet should not stick out.\nThe flat outside a wooden Shield must be covered with leather or fabric.\nThe handles must be made of leather.\nWooden Buckler and Heater Shield with a central handle must have a handle made of wood.\nShield boss (umbo) made of metal must conform to the “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” document.",
      "page_from": 5,
      "page_to": 5,
      "stable_key": "shields-and-bucklers:4",
