    {
      "ordinal": 6,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "5",
      "title": "Metal Shields Requirements",
      "body": "Must be of round shapes, based on historical sources, and repeat the form of the original in all three dimensions.\nThe entire edge of metal Shields must be rolled to the thickness of a minimum of 4 mm or more.\nThe handles must be made of metal and or wood Metal Shield and Shield boss (umbo) must conform to the “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” document.\nIt is allowed to blacken the back part of a metal Shield or metal Buckler.\nExample:\n\nPicture from O. Haguenstein ©",
