      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "6.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "The Heater Shield the main Shield shape for knights of the Middle Ages. Its triangular shape is typical of the 14th century. The shape goes thinner as the armors become more effective.\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nShield of Loew von Steinfurth - 1380 - Germany Grande Chroniques de France - 1400 - France\n\nPolitica & Economica - 1376 - France Ab Urbe Condita - 1390/1400 - France",
