    {
      "ordinal": 14,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "7.2",
      "title": "Specific Requirements",
      "body": "Punch Shield must:\n● conform to the General Requirements and Wooden Shield requirements (see Sections 3 and 4 above),\n● be made of wood,\n● have a shape rectangular, oval or pointed:\n\n● be curved, not flat:\n\n○ Except for Pavese shape, that can be flat if they conform to historical designs:\n\n● have a length of 55 cm to 75 cm,\n● have a width of 30 cm to 50 cm,\n● have handles made of leather (see example in 6.2. Punch Shield).\n\nThe striking area can be rounded or flat.\nThe rounded striking area must conform to a curve of 7 cm diameter.\nFlat striking area must be 7 cm wide as a minimum.\n\n7 cm wide\n\nIt is not allowed to add a Shield boss (umbo) on a Punch Shield.\nIt is allowed to add a metal sheet on the Shield to increase its resilience. In this case:\n● Additional metal sheets must be covered by leather or fabric as another part of the outside of the Shield.\n● Additional metal sheets must have no sharp edges nor pointy parts.\n● Additional metal sheets must be properly attached to the wooden core of the Shield, by rivets, nails or strong glue.",
